<%#
  One answered step, collapsed.

  Reads the entry and only the entry. Steps get edited and deleted after runs,
  so a row built from the live Step record would replay a call with text nobody
  ever saw, or fail on a uuid that no longer resolves.

  Single line on purpose: this is a scanning surface, and a run pays for
  two-line rows in how much of the call stays visible at once.

  locals: entry
%>
<% summary = runner_row_summary(entry) %>
<li class="runner-thread__row" style="--thread-depth: <%= runner_thread_indent(entry) %>;">
  <span class="runner-thread__title"><%= entry["step_title"] %></span>
  <% if summary.present? %>
    <span class="runner-thread__summary"><%= summary %></span>
  <% end %>
</li>
